#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# function_meromorphic

#% text
# `function_meromorphic(f, z)` gives `true` when `f` is meromorphic in the complex variable `z` (analytic except at poles), and `false` when it is not; `function_meromorphic([f, cond], z)` asks where `cond` holds.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The singular points of `f` that are not poles (branch points and cuts, functions analytic nowhere such as `abs` and `re`) must miss the region.

#% item
# Poles come from negative powers, `tan`, `sec`, `csc`, `cot` and their hyperbolic forms, the gamma family, `zeta`.

#% item
# Several variables, parameters (`conditional_expression(true, c)`) and the options of `function_continuous` are accepted.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
function_meromorphic(tan(x), x)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
function_meromorphic(log(x), x)
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The logarithm away from its cut, its zero a pole of the quotient:

#% cell
function_meromorphic([tanh(x)/log(x), re(x) > 0], x)
#% output
#= true

#% text
# The square root in the upper half plane:

#% cell
function_meromorphic([sqrt(z), im_part(z) > 0], z)
#% output
#= true

#% text
# Two variables:

#% cell
[function_meromorphic(pochhammer(x, y), [x, y]), function_meromorphic(x^y, [x, y])]
#% output
#= [true, false]

#% text
# The incomplete gamma function where its argument has a positive real part:

#% cell
function_meromorphic([gamma(x, y), re(y) > 0], [x, y])
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# The cut of `log(z + a)` misses the right half plane when `re(a) >= 0`:

#% cell
function_meromorphic([log(z + a), re(z) > 0], z)
#% output
#= conditional_expression(true, re(a) >= 0)

#% cell
function_meromorphic(sin(z)^a, z, assumptions: element(a, positive_integers))
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Functions with jumps or kinks are not meromorphic:

#% cell
[function_meromorphic(unit_step(x), x), function_meromorphic(abs(z), z)]
#% output
#= [false, false]

#% text
# The poles of a meromorphic function:

#% cell
function_poles(tan(x), x)
#% output
#= [[conditional_expression((1/2)*pi + pi*c(1), element(c(1), integers)), 1]]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A power with a symbolic exponent stays unevaluated; give the exponent's type:

#% cell
[function_meromorphic(z^a, z), function_meromorphic(z^a, z, assumptions: element(a, integers))]
#% output
#= [function_meromorphic(z^a, z), true]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `function_poles`, `function_analytic`, `function_singularities`, `function_continuous`
